# clang-format config for Slate (Objective-C).
#
# No `Language:` key on purpose: a keyless section defaults to Cpp, which
# clang-format also applies to .m/Objective-C files. An `ObjC`-only section is
# rejected ("Unsuitable") for the C-style headers that have no @interface
# (e.g. CarbonCompat.h, SlateLogger.h), which would break the pre-commit hook.
#
# Tuned to match the existing code so adoption stays low-churn:
#   - 2-space indent, attached (K&R) braces  -> Google base
#   - right-aligned pointers (NSString *foo) -> PointerAlignment: Right
#   - lines run long; don't rewrap them      -> ColumnLimit: 0
#   - don't reorder #imports                 -> SortIncludes: false
#
# Pin invocations to Xcode's clang-format (xcrun -f clang-format) so output is
# deterministic regardless of any Homebrew clang-format on $PATH.
---
BasedOnStyle: Google
IndentWidth: 2
ColumnLimit: 0
DerivePointerAlignment: false
PointerAlignment: Right
SortIncludes: false
